  "verbalization": "Omarigliptin is associated with Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus through a chain of indications that link it to other drugs known to influence glucose regulation. The evidence suggests that Omarigliptin may act as a potential therapeutic agent for diabetes, as it is indicated for Diabetes Mellitus, which in turn is linked to several other drugs, including Teneligliptin and Trelagliptin, both of which are known to affect glucose metabolism. The high scores in the paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship between Omarigliptin and the disease, likely due to its pharmacological profile that may influence insulin secretion or glucose uptake. The presence of multiple pathways pointing to the same disease suggests that Omarigliptin could be a candidate for repurposing in the treatment of Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus, though further studies are needed to confirm its efficacy and mechanism of action.",
